    <h2 id="authentication">Authentication</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">DarkLion APIs support two authentication methods: JWT tokens (for the web app) and API keys (for Emma and external integrations). For Emma, always use an API key.</p>

    <div class="auth-box">
      <strong style="color:#c9a84c;">API Key Authentication</strong><br>
      Include your API key in the <code>Authorization</code> header as a Bearer token.<br><br>
      <code>Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here</code>
    </div>
    <div class="auth-box">
      <strong style="color:#c9a84c;">Remote MCP OAuth 2.1</strong><br>
      MCP clients connect to <code>https://your-darklion.example/mcp</code> using Authorization Code with mandatory S256 PKCE. OAuth tokens are bound to that exact resource, firm, active staff identity, client, and granted <code>darklion:read</code>, <code>darklion:write</code>, and <code>darklion:communicate</code> scopes. They are not general API credentials.
    </div>

    <p>API keys are generated in <strong>Settings → API Keys</strong>. Keys start with <code>dlk_</code> and are shown only once at creation — store them securely. For Agent Work endpoints, assign the key to the staff/agent identity it should act as.</p>
    <div class="auth-box">
      <strong style="color:#c9a84c;">Staff-scoped agent calls</strong><br>
      Agent Work endpoints are scoped to the staff/agent identity assigned to the API key in Settings → API Keys. Older general endpoints that support staff scoping may still accept <code>staff_user_id</code> where documented.<br><br>
      <code>Authorization: Bearer dlk_staff_scoped_key</code>
    </div>
    <div class="auth-box">
      <strong style="color:#c9a84c;">Connected-agent callback tokens</strong><br>
      Agent callback endpoints do not use <code>dlk_</code> API keys. They authenticate with the per-connection <code>dla_...</code> callback token in <code>X-DarkLion-Agent-Token</code> or <code>X-Agent-Token</code>. Callback tokens are tied to one staff user's connected agent and cannot be read back after creation.
    </div>

    <h2 id="base-url">Base URL</h2>
    <p>All API endpoints are relative to:</p>
    <pre>https://your-darklion.example</pre>
    <p>Or your firm's custom subdomain if configured (e.g., <code>https://my.yourfirm.com</code>).</p>

    <h2 id="errors">Errors</h2>
    <p>The API uses standard HTTP status codes. Error responses return JSON:</p>
    <pre>{ "error": "Human-readable error message" }</pre>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>400</td><td>Bad request — missing or invalid parameters</td></tr>
        <tr><td>401</td><td>Unauthorized — invalid or missing API key</td></tr>
        <tr><td>403</td><td>Forbidden — you don't have access to this resource</td></tr>
        <tr><td>404</td><td>Not found — resource doesn't exist</td></tr>
        <tr><td>500</td><td>Server error — something went wrong on our end</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="emma-context">Emma Context & Deep Dive Endpoints</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Emma has three layers of data access: firm-wide context for briefings, relationship deep dives for client-specific questions, engagement letter contract data, and full message thread contents.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma/context</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Firm-wide snapshot for morning briefings. Pipeline, unsigned returns, stalled messages, proposals, new clients, expiring engagements, birthdays.</p>

    <h3 id="emma-relationship"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma/relationship/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Everything about a specific relationship: people, companies, active engagement letter contract terms (monthly fees, services, term end date), message threads with last message preview, tax deliveries with signer status, proposals, and documents. Use this when a user asks about a specific client.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Response Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>relationship</td><td>object</td><td>Relationship record</td></tr>
        <tr><td>people</td><td>array</td><td>All people with contact info and portal status</td></tr>
        <tr><td>companies</td><td>array</td><td>All companies with EIN and entity type</td></tr>
        <tr><td>contracts</td><td>array</td><td>Active engagement letters with monthly_line_items, total_monthly, services, term_end_date, ai_summary</td></tr>
        <tr><td>messages</td><td>array</td><td>Recent threads with last message body and unread count</td></tr>
        <tr><td>tax_deliveries</td><td>array</td><td>Tax returns with signer status (signed/approved)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>proposals</td><td>array</td><td>Recent proposals with monthly price</td></tr>
        <tr><td>documents</td><td>array</td><td>Recent documents by year/category</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="emma-engagements"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma/engagement-letters</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">All active engagement letters across the entire firm, with full extracted contract data: client name, services elected, monthly line items, total monthly fee, one-time fees, term end date, and AI summary. Use this to answer billing and contract questions.</p>

    <h3 id="emma-messages"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma/messages/:threadId</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Full contents of a message thread — every message in order with sender type (staff/client), body, and timestamps. Get thread IDs from <code>/api/emma/relationship/:id</code> or <code>/api/messages</code>.</p>

    <h3 id="emma-context-old"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma/context</span> (detail)</h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Returns a comprehensive snapshot of the firm for Emma's daily briefing. No parameters required.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma/context</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Returns a comprehensive snapshot of the firm for Emma's daily briefing. No parameters required.</p>
    <p><strong>Response fields:</strong></p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>firm_summary</td><td>object</td><td>Total counts: relationships, people, companies, open threads, MRR</td></tr>
        <tr><td>pipeline.by_stage</td><td>object</td><td>Pipeline jobs grouped by stage name, each with entity/relationship info</td></tr>
        <tr><td>pipeline.total_active</td><td>number</td><td>Total active pipeline jobs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>urgent.unsigned_tax_returns</td><td>array</td><td>Tax returns sent but not yet signed, with days waiting</td></tr>
        <tr><td>urgent.stalled_messages</td><td>array</td><td>Message threads with no staff reply for 48+ hours</td></tr>
        <tr><td>urgent.open_proposals</td><td>array</td><td>Proposals in sent/viewed status</td></tr>
        <tr><td>needs_attention.new_clients_no_pipeline</td><td>array</td><td>New relationships (last 30 days) with no pipeline job</td></tr>
        <tr><td>needs_attention.expiring_engagements</td><td>array</td><td>Engagement letters expiring within 60 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>needs_attention.birthdays_this_month</td><td>array</td><td>Clients with birthdays this month</td></tr>
        <tr><td>recent_activity</td><td>array</td><td>Tax delivery activity in the last 7 days</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="relationships-list">Relationships</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Relationships are the top-level client groupings. Each relationship can have multiple people and companies attached to it.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/relationships</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List all relationships for the firm. Supports search and filtering.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>search</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter by relationship name</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="relationships-get"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/relationships/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get a single relationship with all associated people and companies.</p>

    <h3 id="relationships-snapshot"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/relationships/:id/snapshot</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get a rich snapshot of a relationship including recent tax deliveries, message threads, activity feed, and active engagement letters.</p>

    <h2 id="people-list">People</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Individual people attached to relationships. People can be portal users, signers on tax returns, and message recipients.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/people</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List all people for the firm.</p>

    <h3 id="people-get"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/people/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get a single person with full details.</p>

    <h3 id="people-update"><span class="method method-put">PUT</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/people/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Update a person's details. Send only the fields you want to update.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>first_name</td><td>string</td><td>First name</td></tr>
        <tr><td>last_name</td><td>string</td><td>Last name</td></tr>
        <tr><td>email</td><td>string</td><td>Email address</td></tr>
        <tr><td>phone</td><td>string</td><td>Phone number</td></tr>
        <tr><td>notes</td><td>string</td><td>Internal staff notes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>portal_enabled</td><td>boolean</td><td>Enable/disable portal access</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="companies-list">Companies</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Companies are business entities attached to relationships. Tax deliveries and documents are often associated with companies.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/companies</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List all companies for the firm.</p>

    <h3 id="companies-get"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/companies/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get a single company with full details including linked people.</p>

    <h2 id="messages-list">Messages</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The messaging system uses threads. Each thread belongs to a person and contains a history of messages between staff and client.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/messages</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List message threads.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>person_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter by person</td></tr>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>open | closed</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="messages-reply"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/messages/:threadId/reply</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Send a reply to an existing message thread.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>body</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Message body text</td></tr>
        <tr><td>internal</td><td>boolean <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>If true, message is internal note only (not sent to client)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="messages-create"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/messages</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Create a new message thread.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>person_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Person to message</td></tr>
        <tr><td>subject</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Thread subject</td></tr>
        <tr><td>body</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Initial message body</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="global-inbox">Global Inbox API</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The inbox API is staff-scoped. Staff JWT requests automatically use the logged-in staff user. API-token requests must pass <code>staff_user_id</code> so agents only inspect one staff member’s assigned inbox at a time. Threads are matched against <code>message_threads.staff_user_id</code> / <code>assigned_to</code>; archived threads are hidden unless explicitly requested by status or <code>include_archived=true</code>.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/inbox</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List recent inbox threads assigned to the scoped staff user, sorted by latest message descending.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>staff_user_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">API token only</span></td><td>Required for API-token auth; ignored for staff JWT auth, which uses the logged-in user.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>limit</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>1-100, default 50</td></tr>
        <tr><td>offset</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Pagination offset, default 0</td></tr>
        <tr><td>search</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Search subject, client name/email, relationship name, or message body</td></tr>
        <tr><td>from_email</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter by client/person email</td></tr>
        <tr><td>unread</td><td>boolean <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>true for threads with unread client messages</td></tr>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter by status, e.g. <code>open</code>, <code>resolved</code>, or <code>archived</code>. If omitted, archived threads are excluded.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>include_archived</td><td>boolean <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to include archived threads when no explicit status filter is passed.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>{
  "threads": [{
    "thread_id": 44,
    "relationship_id": 25,
    "client_name": "Jane Smith",
    "person_name": "Jane Smith",
    "subject": "Tax return question",
    "last_message_preview": "Thanks, I uploaded it...",
    "last_message_at": "2026-05-02T10:00:00.000Z",
    "unread_count": 1,
    "status": "open"
  }],
  "pagination": { "limit": 50, "offset": 0, "count": 1, "total": 1 }
}</pre>

    <h3 id="inbox-thread-detail"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/inbox/threads/:id?staff_user_id=123</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Fetch one thread by ID with all messages and client/relationship context, only if assigned to the scoped staff user. API-token auth must pass <code>staff_user_id</code>. Returns thread metadata plus ordered messages, including internal-note flags.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-put">PUT</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/inbox/threads/:id/archive?staff_user_id=123</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Archive an inbox thread assigned to the scoped staff user. Staff JWT requests use the logged-in user; API-token agents must pass <code>staff_user_id</code>. Returns <code>{ ok: true, thread_id, subject, status: "archived" }</code>.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/inbox/messages/:id?staff_user_id=123</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Fetch one message by ID with thread, client, and relationship context, only if its thread is assigned to the scoped staff user. API-token auth must pass <code>staff_user_id</code>. Use this when an agent has a message ID but not the parent thread ID.</p>

    <h2 id="summaries-month">Conversation Summaries</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Daily conversation summaries show what happened in other staff inboxes. API-token callers must pass <code>staff_user_id</code>; DarkLion returns the same scoped view that staff user sees in the UI, excluding that staff member's own threads to avoid duplicating their inbox.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/summaries?month=YYYY-MM&amp;staff_user_id=123</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Returns calendar rows for days with visible summarized conversations for the scoped staff user.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Query Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>month</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Month in <code>YYYY-MM</code> format. Defaults to the current month.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>staff_user_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-required">required for API keys</span></td><td>Staff user whose summary view should be used. JWT staff users are scoped automatically.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>[{ "date": "2026-05-03", "viewed": false, "thread_count": 4 }]</pre>

    <h3 id="summaries-date"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/summaries/:date?staff_user_id=123</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Fetches a daily summary for the scoped staff user. The response excludes that staff member's own conversations, recomputes <code>thread_count</code>, and marks the summary viewed for that staff user. Summary detail contains <code>summary_json.by_staff</code>, with each visible staff block containing staff name/id and summarized threads (<code>thread_id</code>, client name, subject, bullet summary, message count).</p>
    <pre>{
  "summary_json": {
    "date": "2026-05-03",
    "thread_count": 2,
    "by_staff": [{
      "staff_user_id": 2,
      "staff_name": "Nick",
      "threads": [{ "thread_id": 44, "client_name": "Jane Smith", "subject": "Tax question", "bullets": "• Client uploaded documents" }]
    }]
  }
}</pre>

    <h2 id="agent-connections">Staff-Owned Agent Connections</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Agent connections let each logged-in staff member connect their own external agent to DarkLion. Management endpoints require staff JWT authentication and are scoped to the current staff user; API-token-only auth is rejected. Callback endpoints use the per-connection callback token, not a staff JWT. DarkLion stores agent secrets encrypted and never returns callback token hashes or auth secrets.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-connections/mine</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Returns the current staff user's saved agent connection, or <code>null</code> if none exists. Secrets and callback token hashes are never returned.</p>
    <p>Response: <code>{ connection }</code></p>

    <h3 id="agent-connection-save"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-connections/mine</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Create or update the current staff user's connection. The callback token is returned only when the connection is first created or <code>rotate_callback_token</code> is true; store it in the external agent because it cannot be read back later.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>agent_name</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Display name for the connected staff agent.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>provider</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Provider label, defaults to <code>webhook</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>endpoint_url</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>External agent endpoint DarkLion can call in future wake/chat flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>auth_type</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td><code>none</code> | <code>bearer</code> | <code>api_key</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>auth_secret</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Stored encrypted when <code>auth_type</code> is not <code>none</code>. Omit to keep the existing secret on update.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>session_key</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>External session/thread identifier.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td><code>connected</code> | <code>paused</code> | <code>disabled</code> | <code>error</code>. Defaults to <code>paused</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>capabilities</td><td>object <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Boolean flags. Existing flags include <code>chat</code>, <code>inbox_drafts</code>, <code>summaries</code>, <code>tasks</code>. Agent Work API flags default enabled unless explicitly set false: <code>inbox_read</code>, <code>inbox_drafts</code>, <code>team_chat_read</code>, <code>team_chat_send</code>, <code>activity_log_read</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>preferences_json</td><td>object <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Staff-specific agent preferences.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>rotate_callback_token</td><td>boolean <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>When true, issues a new <code>dla_...</code> callback token and invalidates the old one.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>{
  "connection": {
    "id": 12,
    "agent_name": "Emma",
    "provider": "webhook",
    "status": "connected",
    "callback_token": "dla_returned_only_on_create_or_rotation"
  }
}</pre>

    <h3><span class="method method-patch">PATCH</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-connections/mine/status</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Enable, pause, or disable the current staff user's connection.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td><code>connected</code> | <code>paused</code> | <code>disabled</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="agent-callback-inbox-draft"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-callbacks/inbox-draft</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Preferred callback URL for connected staff agents to post a suggested inbox reply draft into DarkLion. The alias <code>/api/agent-connections/callbacks/inbox-draft</code> exists for compatibility, but <code>/api/agent-callbacks/inbox-draft</code> is the documented contract.</p>
    <p>Authenticate with the callback token in <code>X-DarkLion-Agent-Token</code> (or <code>X-Agent-Token</code>). The matching connection must be <code>connected</code>, and the target thread must belong to that staff user.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>thread_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Message thread ID assigned to the connected staff user.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>draft_body</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Suggested reply text to show in the staff inbox.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>confidence</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Agent confidence score, if available.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>notes</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Internal notes shown with the draft. <code>agent_notes</code> is also accepted.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>curl -X POST https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-callbacks/inbox-draft \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-DarkLion-Agent-Token: dla_your_callback_token" \
  -d '{"thread_id":123,"draft_body":"Suggested client reply","confidence":0.87}'</pre>
    <p>Success response: <code>{ "ok": true, "draft_id": 456 }</code></p>

    <h3 id="agent-chat-callback"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-callbacks/chat-reply</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Async chat callback for connected agents. When DarkLion sends a <code>chat.message.received</code> wake to the connected agent, the payload includes <code>chat_message_id</code> and a <code>callback_url</code>. Post the final answer here to replace the in-app “sent to agent” placeholder and push the answer live via Pusher.</p>
    <p>Authenticate with <code>X-DarkLion-Agent-Token</code> or <code>X-Agent-Token</code>. The connection must be <code>connected</code>.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>chat_message_id</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>ID from the original wake payload.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>reply</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Final assistant reply. Aliases accepted: <code>message</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>content</code>, <code>response</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>curl -X POST https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-callbacks/chat-reply \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-DarkLion-Agent-Token: dla_your_callback_token" \
  -d '{"chat_message_id":"msg_abc123","reply":"Here is the answer..."}'</pre>
    <p>Success response: <code>{ "ok": true }</code>. Duplicate callbacks for the same <code>chat_message_id</code> return <code>{ "ok": true, "duplicate": true }</code>.</p>

    <h3 id="agent-drafts"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-connections/drafts/:threadId</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List pending agent drafts for a thread visible to the current staff user. Staff JWT only.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-connections/drafts/:threadId/generate</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Manually request a native Emma draft for a visible inbox thread. Queues an <code>emma_draft_jobs</code> worker job and returns <code>202 Accepted</code> with the queued job. The worker gathers thread history, client/relationship profile, documents, extracted tax data, bookkeeping context, Blueleaf snapshots, and pipeline/work context before creating a pending <code>message_drafts</code> record. Staff JWT only.</p>
    <p>Response: <code>{ "job": { "id": 123, "status": "queued", "thread_id": 44 } }</code></p>

    <h3><span class="method method-patch">PATCH</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-connections/drafts/:draftId</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Update a pending draft after staff review.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td><code>pending</code> | <code>accepted</code> | <code>edited_sent</code> | <code>discarded</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="agent-work">Agent Work API</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Agent Work endpoints let a staff agent poll DarkLion on a schedule without being woken by DarkLion. They authenticate with normal <code>dlk_...</code> API keys from Settings → API Keys. The key must be assigned to the staff/agent identity it should act as. V1 allows live firm revenue forecasting, firm-wide activity log review, Inbox read + draft creation for client-facing messages, Team Chat read + direct internal replies, and fast company transaction search.</p>

    <div class="auth-box">
      <strong style="color:#c9a84c;">Agent Work Auth</strong><br>
      <code>Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here</code><br><br>
      The API key must be assigned to a Staff / Agent Identity in Settings → API Keys. Every request is written to <code>agent_audit_events</code>. Polling read endpoints do not mark Inbox or Team Chat messages as read.
    </div>

    <h3 id="remote-mcp">Remote MCP + OAuth</h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">The remote MCP exposes 62 narrow tools across supported CRM, documents, work, communications, bookkeeping records, tax records, proposals, billing configuration, investments, engagement letters, transactions, Inbox, and Team Chat operations. OAuth discovery is available at <code>/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp</code> and <code>/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server</code>. Client send/reply requires the separate <code>darklion:communicate</code> grant; existing connections must reconnect and re-authorize.</p>

    <h3 id="agent-work-companies"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/companies</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List active companies visible to the scoped staff identity. Requires <code>transactions_read</code> and respects staff-level company restrictions. Use the returned <code>id</code> or <code>realm_id</code> with transaction tools.</p>

    <h3 id="agent-work-crm-search"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/crm/search?q=Smith&amp;limit=10</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Search the authorized firm's relationship names, linked people, spouse names, emails, and active companies. Requires <code>crm_read</code>. Results are grouped into <code>relationships</code>, <code>people</code>, and <code>companies</code>; the per-group limit is capped at 25.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/status</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Validate the token and return the scoped firm/staff identity, effective capabilities, and resource-specific notes for endpoints with side effects.</p>
    <pre>curl https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-work/status \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here"</pre>
    <pre>{
  "ok": true,
  "firm_id": 1,
  "staff_user_id": 1,
  "agent_connection_id": null,
  "agent_name": "API Agent",
  "capabilities": {
    "agent_work": true,
    "inbox_read": true,
    "inbox_drafts": true,
    "team_chat_read": true,
    "team_chat_send": true,
    "documents_read": true,
    "activity_log_read": true,
    "transactions_read": true,
    "transactions_write": true,
    "revenue_read": true,
    "general_api": true,
    "summaries_read": true,
    "crm_read": true
  },
  "resources": {
    "summaries": {
      "calendar_read": true,
      "detail_read": true,
      "detail_marks_viewed": false
    },
    "revenue_forecast": {
      "read": true,
      "live_sources": true
    },
    "crm": {
      "search": true
    }
  }
}</pre>
    <p class="endpoint-desc"><code>summaries_read</code> covers the Conversation Summaries calendar and detail endpoints. Both Agent Work adapter reads are side-effect free.</p>

    <h3 id="agent-work-revenue-forecast"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/revenue-forecast?year=2027</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Return the same live recurring-revenue figures used by DarkLion's Revenue Forecast page, with forecast-friendly monthly aggregates. Requires <code>revenue_read</code>. The optional year defaults to the current year and may be up to ten years in the future.</p>
    <pre>curl "https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-work/revenue-forecast?year=2027" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here"</pre>
    <pre>{
  "generated_at": "2026-07-30T14:15:00.000Z",
  "year": 2027,
  "totals": {
    "annual": 312000,
    "collected": 0,
    "pastDue": 0,
    "upcoming": 312000
  },
  "monthly_totals": [{
    "month": "2027-01",
    "collected": 0,
    "past_due": 0,
    "upcoming": 26000,
    "projected": 26000
  }],
  "customers": [{
    "name": "Example Client",
    "source": "stripe",
    "monthlyAmount": 1000,
    "annual": 12000,
    "months": [{ "status": "upcoming", "amount": 1000 }]
  }],
  "assumptions": {
    "sources": ["stripe_active_subscriptions", "stripe_past_due_subscriptions", "aum_billing"],
    "annual_definition": "Current monthly recurring amount multiplied by 12.",
    "projected_definition": "Paid, past-due, or upcoming recurring revenue assigned to each month.",
    "baseline_assumption": "Current recurring amounts continue unchanged; churn, growth, cancellations, and AUM market movement are not modeled.",
    "excludes": ["one_time_revenue", "unsigned_proposals", "non_recurring_qbo_revenue"]
  }
}</pre>
