    <h3 id="agent-work-team-summary"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/team-chat/summary</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Return unread Team Chat counts and unread conversations visible to the connected staff user.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/team-chat/conversations?unread=true&amp;limit=50</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List Team Chat conversations visible to the connected staff user. Use <code>unread=true</code> for polling.</p>

    <h3 id="agent-work-team-messages"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/team-chat/conversations/:conversationId/messages</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Fetch recent Team Chat messages and attachment metadata. This is read-only and does not mark the conversation read.</p>

    <h3 id="agent-work-team-reply"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/team-chat/conversations/:conversationId/reply</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Send an internal Team Chat reply as the connected staff user. This is allowed in v1 because Team Chat is internal.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>body</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>Message text. Aliases accepted: <code>message</code> or <code>text</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>client_nonce</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Idempotency key. If omitted, DarkLion generates one.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>curl -X POST https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-work/team-chat/conversations/12/reply \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here" \
  -d '{"body":"I checked the inbox — two client replies need review."}'</pre>

    <h3 id="agent-work-transaction-search"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/companies/:companyId/transactions/search</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Fast company transaction search for agents. Optimized for vendor/payee and amount filtering across coded transaction history plus latest uncoded bookkeeper review rows. Requires the API key/agent capability <code>transactions_read</code> to not be disabled.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>vendor</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Vendor/payee search. Also checks description and original account text.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>q</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Alias/general text search when vendor is unknown.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>amount</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Exact absolute amount match. Defaults to ±$0.01 tolerance.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>amount_near</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Fuzzy absolute amount match. Defaults to ±5% or ±$1, whichever is greater.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>tolerance</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Override exact/near amount tolerance.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>amount_min</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Minimum absolute amount.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>amount_max</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Maximum absolute amount.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>date_from</td><td>date <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>YYYY-MM-DD lower transaction-date bound.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>date_to</td><td>date <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>YYYY-MM-DD upper transaction-date bound.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter by status, e.g. <code>categorized</code>, <code>pending</code>, <code>coded</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>source</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td><code>transactions</code> or <code>bookkeeper_uncoded</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>include_uncoded</td><td>boolean <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Default true. Set false to search only coded transaction history.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>limit</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Default 25, max 100.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>offset</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Pagination offset.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>curl "https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-work/companies/123/transactions/search?vendor=home%20depot&amp;amount_near=250&amp;tolerance=20&amp;date_from=2025-01-01" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here"</pre>

    <h3><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/transactions/search</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Same search engine as the GET endpoint, but with an agent-friendly JSON body. Use <code>company_id</code> or <code>realm_id</code>.</p>
    <pre>curl -X POST https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-work/transactions/search \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here" \
  -d '{
    "company_id": 29,
    "vendor": "staples",
    "amount": { "near": 75, "tolerance": 15 },
    "date_range": { "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2025-12-31" },
    "limit": 10
  }'</pre>
    <pre>{
  "company": { "id": 29, "realm_id": "9130352500120646", "company_name": "Example Co" },
  "count": 1,
  "total_count": 1,
  "transactions": [{
    "id": 155,
    "source": "transactions",
    "transaction_id": "3178",
    "date": "2025-04-12",
    "vendor": "Staples",
    "amount": 62.18,
    "description": "Staples Office Supplies",
    "original_account": "Uncategorized Expense",
    "coded_account": "Office Supplies",
    "doc_number": "1023",
    "memo": "April rent",
    "qbo_txn_type": "Purchase",
    "status": "categorized"
  }]
}</pre>

    <h3 id="agent-work-transaction-backfill"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/companies/:companyId/transactions/backfill</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Pull historical QBO transactions into DarkLion's searchable transaction table. Use this when search returns no results for a connected company with no local transaction history yet. Requires the API key/agent capability <code>transactions_write</code> to not be disabled.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>months</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Lookback window. Default 24, max 84.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>types</td><td>array <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>QBO entity types to pull. Defaults to Purchase, Bill, Deposit, SalesReceipt, Invoice, Payment, JournalEntry, CreditMemo, VendorCredit, RefundReceipt.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>curl -X POST https://your-darklion.example/api/agent-work/companies/123/transactions/backfill \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer dlk_your_api_key_here" \
  -d '{"months":24}'</pre>
    <pre>{
  "ok": true,
  "company": { "id": 123, "realm_id": "1234567890123456", "company_name": "Example Company" },
  "start_date": "2024-05-13",
  "months": 24,
  "fetched": 214,
  "inserted": 214,
  "updated": 0,
  "errors": [],
  "by_type": { "Purchase": { "fetched": 52, "inserted": 52, "updated": 0 } }
}</pre>

    <h3><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/agent-work/transactions/backfill</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">JSON-body variant. Pass <code>company_id</code> or <code>realm_id</code>, plus optional <code>months</code> and <code>types</code>.</p>

    <h3>Recommended polling flow</h3>
    <pre>Daily or when preparing a forecast:
1. GET /api/agent-work/revenue-forecast?year=YYYY

Every 15 minutes:
1. GET /api/agent-work/activity-log?include_summaries=true
2. GET /api/agent-work/inbox/summary
3. GET /api/agent-work/inbox/threads?unread=true
4. GET /api/agent-work/inbox/threads/:threadId
5. POST /api/agent-work/inbox/threads/:threadId/draft when a client reply is useful
6. GET /api/agent-work/team-chat/summary
7. GET /api/agent-work/team-chat/conversations?unread=true
8. GET /api/agent-work/team-chat/conversations/:conversationId/messages
9. POST /api/agent-work/team-chat/conversations/:conversationId/reply when the agent should answer internally</pre>

    <h2 id="docs-list">Documents</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Documents are stored in S3 and organized by owner (person or company), year, category (tax/other), and section (firm_uploaded or client_uploaded). API responses never expose raw S3 credentials; download/open fields are protected DarkLion URLs that mint short-lived signed S3 links.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/documents</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List documents.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>owner_type</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>person | company. Required with owner_id unless relationship_id is provided.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>owner_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>ID of the person or company. Required with owner_type unless relationship_id is provided.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>relationship_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>List documents for all people and companies in a relationship. Returns <code>{ documents: [...] }</code> with API download URLs.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>year</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter by tax year e.g. "2025"</td></tr>
        <tr><td>category</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Alias for folder_category.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>folder_category</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>tax | other</td></tr>
        <tr><td>folder_section</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>firm_uploaded | client_uploaded</td></tr>
        <tr><td>doc_type</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter by document type when available.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>is_delivered</td><td>boolean <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Filter documents already attached/delivered through tax delivery.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <pre>{
  "documents": [{
    "id": 105,
    "display_name": "2025 Form 1040.pdf",
    "relationship_id": 25,
    "person_name": "Jane Smith",
    "folder_category": "tax",
    "download_url": "/api/documents/105/download",
    "open_url": "/api/documents/105/open"
  }]
}</pre>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/documents/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get metadata for one document, including owner context, relationship context when applicable, and API download/open URLs.</p>
    <p>Response: <code>{ "document": { ... } }</code></p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/documents/:id/download</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Returns a signed S3 download URL for the actual stored file. The response is JSON, not the file bytes: <code>{ "url": "https://..." }</code>. Alias: <code>GET /api/documents/:id/url</code>.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/documents/:id/open</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Redirects directly to the signed S3 URL with HTTP 302. Useful for browser/open-in-new-tab flows.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/documents/:id/extracted_data</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Returns normalized parsed tax data for a PDF document. Uses linked tax delivery report data when available; otherwise extracts and analyzes the actual PDF live. Includes AGI, taxable income, total tax, filing status, tax year, form type, source, and raw extracted JSON.</p>
    <pre>{
  "document_id": 105,
  "extraction_status": "completed",
  "adjusted_gross_income": 120000,
  "taxable_income": 95000,
  "total_tax": 18000,
  "filing_status": "married_filing_jointly",
  "tax_year": "2025",
  "form_type": "1040",
  "source": "tax_delivery_report_data"
}</pre>

    <h3 id="docs-move"><span class="method method-put">PUT</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/documents/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Update document metadata including moving between folders.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>display_name</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Rename the document</td></tr>
        <tr><td>year</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Move to a different tax year folder</td></tr>
        <tr><td>folder_section</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>firm_uploaded | client_uploaded</td></tr>
        <tr><td>folder_category</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>tax | other</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="docs-delete"><span class="method method-delete">DELETE</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/documents/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Permanently delete a document from S3 and the database. If attached to a draft tax delivery, the delivery and attached files are deleted too. If attached to a non-draft/signed delivery, the API returns 409 until the request is repeated with <code>{ "confirm_delete": "DELETE" }</code>. This protects signed/sent delivery records from accidental removal.</p>
    <pre>// first attempt on protected delivery document
{ "error": "Document is attached to a sent/signed tax delivery", "requires_confirmation": true }

// confirmed request body
{ "confirm_delete": "DELETE" }</pre>

    <h2 id="pipeline-jobs">Pipelines</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Pipelines track workflow progress for clients. Each client entity (person or company) can have one or more pipeline jobs moving through stages.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/pipelines/jobs</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List active pipeline jobs. Returns jobs with their current stage, entity, and relationship info.</p>

    <h3 id="pipeline-move"><span class="method method-put">PUT</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/pipelines/jobs/:id</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Update a pipeline job — most commonly used to advance to the next stage.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>current_stage_id</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>ID of the new stage to move the job to</td></tr>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>active | complete | archived</td></tr>
        <tr><td>title</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>Update job title</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>To advance a job to the next stage, you need the stage ID. Get stages for a pipeline template with <code>GET /api/pipelines/templates/:id/stages</code> (see below).</p>

    <h3 id="pipeline-stages"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/pipelines/templates/:id/stages</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List all stages for a pipeline template, ordered by position. Use this to get stage IDs for moving jobs.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>id</td><td>number</td><td>Stage ID — use this in PUT /jobs/:id to move a job</td></tr>
        <tr><td>name</td><td>string</td><td>Stage name (e.g. "CPA Return Review")</td></tr>
        <tr><td>position</td><td>number</td><td>Order in the pipeline (0 = first)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>color</td><td>string</td><td>Stage color for UI display</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="tax-list">Tax Deliveries</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Tax deliveries are the end-to-end workflow for delivering a completed tax return to a client for review and e-signature.</p>

    <p><strong>Delivery statuses:</strong> <code>draft</code> → <code>sent</code> → <code>approved</code> → <code>signed</code> → <code>complete</code>. If changes requested: <code>needs_changes</code>.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/tax-deliveries</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List tax deliveries for a company or person.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>company_id</td><td>number</td><td>Filter by company (use one of these)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>person_id</td><td>number</td><td>Filter by person</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="tax-send"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/tax-deliveries/:id/send</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Send a draft tax delivery to the client. This notifies signers via email and creates a portal message thread. Delivery must be in <code>draft</code> status.</p>

    <h3 id="tax-summary"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/tax-deliveries/:id/summary</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get the AI-generated tax summary for a delivery (if generated).</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>status</td><td>string</td><td>none | processing | completed | error</td></tr>
        <tr><td>data</td><td>object | null</td><td>Full ReportData object when completed (see Tax Summary Schema below)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/tax-deliveries/:id/generate-summary</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Trigger AI analysis of the attached PDF. Runs asynchronously — poll <code>/summary</code> for status. Requires a review document to be attached.</p>

    <h2 id="proposals-list">Proposals</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Proposals are the engagement letter / service agreement workflow. Clients select a tier, provide their info, and e-sign the LOE.</p>

    <p><strong>Proposal statuses:</strong> <code>draft</code> → <code>sent</code> → <code>viewed</code> → <code>accepted</code> → <code>signed</code></p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/proposals</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List all proposals for the firm. Supports filtering by status.</p>

    <h3 id="proposals-stats"><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/proposals/stats</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get proposal statistics: total, sent, accepted/signed, and signed MRR.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>total</td><td>number</td><td>Total proposals</td></tr>
        <tr><td>sent</td><td>number</td><td>Proposals in sent status</td></tr>
        <tr><td>accepted_signed</td><td>number</td><td>Proposals accepted or signed</td></tr>
        <tr><td>mrr</td><td>number</td><td>Monthly recurring revenue from signed engagements</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="emma-context-prompt">Emma Context Prompt</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Emma pushes a structured firm context document to DarkLion on a schedule (overnight deep refresh + hourly during business hours). The built-in Claude assistant reads this context when answering staff questions — so staff get instant responses powered by Emma's deep analysis. Accepts API token auth.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-put">PUT</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/context</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Emma pushes the current firm context prompt. Overwrites the previous version. Claude will use this on every staff message until the next update.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>context</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>The full context document — pipeline status, per-staff tasks, urgent items, client details, staff directory. Can be 5,000–15,000 tokens.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>updated_at</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td><td>ISO timestamp of when this context was generated. Shown to Claude so it knows how fresh the data is.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/context</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Read back the current stored context. Emma uses this to verify what's live and diff against planned updates.</p>
    <p>Response: <code>{ context, updated_at, updated_by }</code></p>

    <h2 id="emma-session">Emma Chat</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The Emma Chat API powers the live AI assistant in the DarkLion dashboard. The live chat currently answers directly through DarkLion's built-in Emma/Claude flow; connected-agent infrastructure remains available for wakes, async callbacks, inbox drafts, and future routing. Sessions are per-user per-day and auto-purge after 3 days. <strong>Note:</strong> Staff-facing session/message endpoints require JWT authentication because Emma needs a <code>userId</code> to store per-user sessions. API token auth is only supported on the explicitly documented <code>*-for/:userId</code> and context endpoints.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/session</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Get or create today's session for the current user. Returns the session record including any existing messages. Also triggers 3-day cleanup of old sessions.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>id</td><td>number</td><td>Session ID</td></tr>
        <tr><td>session_date</td><td>string</td><td>Today's date (YYYY-MM-DD)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>messages</td><td>array</td><td>Array of message objects with role, content, timestamp</td></tr>
        <tr><td>briefing_generated</td><td>boolean</td><td>Whether morning briefing has been generated today</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="emma-briefing"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/briefing</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Generate Emma's morning briefing for today. Pulls full firm context (<code>/api/emma/context</code>), sends to Claude Haiku, and stores the result. Only generates once per day — subsequent calls return the cached briefing.</p>
    <p>No request body required. Response:</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>messages</td><td>array</td><td>Session messages including the new briefing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>already_generated</td><td>boolean</td><td>True if briefing was cached from an earlier call today</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/session-for/:userId</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Emma reads a staff member's current session — all messages sent to and from them today. Use this to monitor what staff are asking and whether Emma's briefings were received. Accepts API token auth.</p>
    <p>Response: <code>{ user, user_id, session_date, messages, briefing_generated }</code></p>

    <h3><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/reply-for/:userId</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Emma injects a message directly into a staff member's chat as if he typed it. The message appears as an assistant bubble in the dashboard. Use this to proactively push updates, answer questions Emma detected via monitoring, or send follow-ups.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>message</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>The message text Emma wants to inject</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/briefing-for/:userId</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Emma uses this to push a personalized morning briefing into a specific staff member's chat session. Accepts API token auth — Emma can call this with his <code>dlk_</code> token. Get user IDs from <code>GET /api/staff</code>. Only generates once per day per user; subsequent calls return the cached briefing.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>userId (path)</td><td>number <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>firm_users.id of the staff member to brief</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Response: <code>{ ok, user, messages, already_generated }</code></p>

    <h3 id="emma-message"><span class="method method-post">POST</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/emma-chat/message</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">Send a message to Emma. Emma receives the current firm context plus recent conversation history, can use approved internal tools, and stores the response in the session. Available tools include scoped inbox lookup, message detail lookup, relationship/document lookup, document extracted tax data, and safe email-style draft generation. Draft tools create suggested copy only; humans still review and send client communications.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>message</td><td>string <span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td><td>The user's message text</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Response:</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>reply</td><td>string</td><td>Emma's response text</td></tr>
        <tr><td>messages</td><td>array</td><td>Full updated conversation history for this session</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="staff-list">Staff</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The staff endpoint returns all accepted firm users. Emma uses this to build per-staff task lists and assignments.</p>

    <h3><span class="method method-get">GET</span> <span class="endpoint-path">/api/staff</span></h3>
    <p class="endpoint-desc">List all accepted staff users for the firm.</p>
    <table class="params-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>id</td><td>number</td><td>User ID</td></tr>
        <tr><td>name</td><td>string</td><td>Full name</td></tr>
        <tr><td>display_name</td><td>string</td><td>Display/preferred name</td></tr>
        <tr><td>email</td><td>string</td><td>Email address</td></tr>
        <tr><td>role</td><td>string</td><td>owner | admin | staff</td></tr>
        <tr><td>last_login_at</td><td>string</td><td>Last login timestamp</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

